<title>GERMANY: W.German 1997 industry output seen up - Ifo.</title>
<headline>W.German 1997 industry output seen up - Ifo.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ifo economic research institute said in its latest &quot;Forecast 100&quot; survey published on Sunday that western German manufacturers now expect a stronger rise in industry output next year.</p>
<p>Ifo published the following detailed forecasts for production in the west German manufacturing sector. All figures in percent, previous forecast in brackets,</p>
<p>					    1996		  1997</p>
<p> Manufacturing industry	+0.25 (+0.75)     +1.5  (+1.25)</p>
<p>Of which,</p>
<p> Basic, producer goods	 -0.25 (+0.50)     +1.25 (+1.25)</p>
<p> Capital goods		   +0.5  (+1.0)	+2.0  (+1.0)</p>
<p> Consumer goods		  UNCH  (+0.5)	+1.0  (+1.5)</p>
<p> Food, luxury goods	    +0.50 (+1.0)	+1.0  (+1.5)</p>
<p>NOTE - Current forecasts based on survey conducted with emphasis on September and previous forecasts on January.</p>
<p>Ifo said in its next survey it would adopt the harmonised European Union reporting method for industry output.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, +49 228 26097150</p>
